A table renamed is, to SQLite's listings, one table gone and another new:
refused, since the old one's rows would go. There is no rename.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'soup');

== after
CREATE TABLE meal (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== error
table `dish` is in the database, not in schema.sql: its rows would go. Keep it, or drop it on purpose: `-- @drop table dish` in schema.sql. (A rename is a drop and a new one: the rows do not follow.)
